From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RTSP-on-GE design <rtsp-on-ge@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 16:47:31 -0500
Subject: [PATCH alpha 2/4] winedmo: make direct network demux teardown
 interruptible

Install FFmpeg interrupt callbacks for direct HLS and RTSP inputs, expose a cancellation call across the Unix boundary, and order media-source flush and shutdown so the worker is joined before the demuxer is destroyed.

Bound RTSP open/probe operations to 30 seconds and RTSP read/seek/close operations to 15 seconds. HLS receives cancellation support without a new steady-state I/O deadline, preserving GE playback behavior.

Report demuxer seekability to Media Foundation, avoid the synthetic
seek-to-zero for live/unseekable streams, and discard any packet whose read or
queue handoff overlapped a flush instead of re-queuing stale pre-seek data.
